/-!
# P-256 field-multiply leaf value ↔ in-Lean and fiat-crypto theorem index

Citation table for the field-multiply denotation in
`CatCrypt/Crypto/Vale/P256FieldMul.lean`. The leaf value is grounded in Lean:
`P256_fmul_denote` is `Number.montgomeryReduce` at the P-256 prime, and
`P256_fmul_denote_spec` / `P256_fmul_denote_runBlock` prove it is the
Montgomery product `x · y · R⁻¹ mod p` computed by the emitted 256×256→512
product block (`Curve4LimbTierA.p256_emit_montmul_runBlock`,
`Number.montgomeryMul_correct`). The fiat-crypto row below is the
cross-prover corroboration of that same value. Parallel to
`CatCrypt/Crypto/KeyAgreement/X25519/CoqAxioms.lean`.

## Field / prime

NIST P-256 base field, `p = 2^256 − 2^224 + 2^192 + 2^96 − 1`
= `0xffffffff00000001000000000000000000000000ffffffffffffffffffffffff`
= `115792089210356248762697446949407573530086143415290314195533631308867097853951`.
The fiat-crypto `fiat_p256_mul` is generated by
`word_by_word_montgomery --lang Rust p256 64 '2^256 - 2^224 + 2^192 + 2^96 - 1'`
into `fiat-crypto/fiat-rust/src/p256_64.rs`; the Rust wrapper is
`p256-safe-rust/src/lib.rs::fp_mul` (C ABI `p256_fp_mul`). This is the
same `fiat_p256_mul` the `Pairing/P256GroupEmit.lean` point-add routes
to. Montgomery radix `R = 2^256`, 4×u64 saturated limbs (32 bytes).

## Status legend

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| proved | the cited fiat-crypto theorem is `Qed`-closed |
| cited | the citation is the cross-prover trust boundary |

## Field arithmetic (Fp_{P-256})

| Lean value | In-Lean grounding | fiat-crypto corroboration |
|---|---|---|
| `P256_fmul_denote` | `P256_fmul_denote_spec`: on reduced inputs, `denote x y < 2·p` and `(denote x y) · 2^256 ≡ x · y (mod p)`. `P256_fmul_denote_runBlock`: `denote (valLimbs x) (valLimbs y)` is `Number.montgomeryReduce` of the emitted product block's `runBlock` value, via `Curve4LimbTierA.p256_emit_montmul_runBlock` and `Number.montgomeryMul_correct`. | `fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/WordByWordMontgomery.v::mulmod_correct` (`Qed`): `eval (from_montgomerymod (mulmod a b)) mod m = (eval (from_montgomerymod a) * eval (from_montgomerymod b)) mod m` for `valid a`, `valid b`, at `m = p_{P-256}`. C-operation form: `fiat-crypto/src/COperationSpecifications.v` module `WordByWordMontgomery`, `mul_correct`. Realized leaf: `fiat_p256_mul` in `fiat-crypto/fiat-rust/src/p256_64.rs`; Montgomery product `x · y · R⁻¹ mod p`, `R = 2^256`. |

